  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishing and conserving a population of Bornean orangutans (Pongo pygmaeus) in Bukit Baka Bukit Raya National Park, through capacity building, education and community engagement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will accomplish the following objectives: (1) Implement the conservation management plan developed in the previous stages of the project to protect reintroduced orangutans, focusing on understanding hunting pressures in and around the National Park; (2) Continue to conduct pre-release and post-release monitoring of orangutans to contribute to a newly established wild orangutan population and the first comprehensive behavioral data set of reintroduced orangutans in west Kalimantan; (3) Conduct participatory mapping of the community traditional area of Mentatai resort in BBBRNP to support sustainable development of the local communities; (4) Determine land use patterns in the areas around the three villages and optimize the use of available land to reduce further encroachment in the park; (5) Develop cooperation with the local communities to protect orangutan and other key species through the revitalization of customary law (Peraturan Adat and Peraturan Desa) to increase support for the park&apos;s protection and reduce the risk for any potential threats to the reintroduced orangutans; and, (6) Establish a forest patrol team, made up of BBBR NP staff and local community members, to monitor threats to the park and ensure the protection of the forest and reintroduced orangutans.</narrative>
  </description>
